# Every file is checked out byte for byte on every platform.
#
# Windows runners ship core.autocrlf=true, which would otherwise rewrite line
# endings on the way out of git. Two things here cannot survive that: the
# release verification digests the assembly each platform compiles the fixture
# corpus to and requires the three to be identical, which a rewritten fixture
# would make a property of the checkout rather than of the compiler; and
# .llvm-version is read by a shell, which would take the carriage return as part
# of the version.
* -text
